{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210737,"nonce":"T8CdXDrZ5Dq/2VRqNSr90fXIAlk=","title":"the_strangler GLTF load hung: native ByteArray bulk decoders","message":"Fixed; see git log for the landing commit. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n**RESOLVED 2026-06-03.** `the_strangler` (CC-BY by Jungle Jim, 63 MB scene.bin, 102 joints, 315 anim channels, 245k+ input / 630k+ output frames) loads in ~40s; previously hung indefinitely.\n\n1. `Bytes_.f32LE` in `hatch-gltf/gltf.wren` reconstructed every IEEE-754 float in pure Wren with `2.pow(exp - 127)` per call. ~876k of those calls just for animation data.\n2. `FS.readBytes` returned `List\u003cNum\u003e` — one tagged-double Value per byte. 63 MB file = 63 million List entries before parsing even started.\n\n- **Native bulk decoders on `ByteArray`** (`src/runtime/core/typed_array.rs`):\n  - `readF32LE(byteOffset)`, `readU16LE`, `readU32LE` — scalar native readers.\n  - `copyToFloat32Array(srcOff, count, dst, dstOff, stride)` — bulk decode into a `Float32Array`. One FFI per accessor.\n  - `copyU16LEToInt32Array(...)`, `copyU8ToInt32Array(...)` — bulk widening for index / joint accessors.\n- **`FS.readBytes` now returns `ByteArray`** (`src/runtime/core/fs.rs`). Single u8 Vec allocation regardless of file size. `FS.writeBytes` accepts both `ByteArray` and `List\u003cNum\u003e` so existing callers still work.\n- `hatch-gltf/gltf.wren` switched `readFloatAccessor_` / `readU16x4Accessor_` / `readIndexAccessor_` to the bulk path (one FFI per accessor when tightly packed, one per row when strided).\n\n- the_strangler: hangs → 42s end-to-end load (mostly PNG decoding of 26 textures + GPU upload now).\n- All `hatch-fs` / `hatch-gltf` / `hatch-gpu` / `hatch-game` specs green after the change.\n- `Fs.readBytes(p).toList` for List-equality compares; otherwise indexed + iteration access works identically to before.\n\n- `wlift_image` (PNG decode) is now the dominant cost — texture-heavy scenes benefit from async / parallel decode.\n- Bulk `copyU32LEToInt32Array` for the rare u32 index path.\n- `mmap`-backed `Assets.bytes(path)` for zero-copy file → ByteArray (no allocation at all). Useful once asset sizes exceed available RAM.","files":null}]}